# Normalize line endings to LF for everything Git treats as text, regardless
# of the OS or editor that touches it, or what a local core.autocrlf setting
# says. Without this, Windows checkouts convert to CRLF on disk while this
# project's files (including anything delivered as a fresh export) stay LF,
# which makes `git status`/`git diff` flag nearly the whole repo as
# "modified" even when no real content changed — see the false-positive diff
# noise this was added to fix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders: a few types that should never be reinterpreted as text
# even if extensions are guessed wrong.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
